What:		/sys/bus/spmi/devices/<dev>/hib_resume
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.4
Contact:	František Balázsy <frantisekbalazsy@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RW) How the last resume from hibernation left an Apple
		SN201202x USB Type-C port controller. Reads one of:

		none
			No resume from hibernation since the last system
			sleep, or "roles" was written since.
		roles-pending
			The controller was restored in place after the cold
			boot behind the resume. The kernel revalidates the
			port, without taking the port or a display on it
			down, once the USB controller that provides its role
			switch is bound.
		failed
			The in-place restore failed; the controller has to be
			probed again (unbind and bind the device).

		Writing "roles" while the state is "roles-pending" takes note
		of it: the state then reads "none". The write is not needed
		for the port to be revalidated. Other values fail with
		-EINVAL, a write in another state with -EALREADY.
